{"page":2,"totalPages":4,"perPage":6,"nextPage":3,"html":"<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/watch-movement.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/watch-movement.webp\" alt=\"A close-up of the escapement: a gilt balance wheel with timing screws around its rim and a blued hairspring coiled inside it, the steel pallet fork beside it, and the escape wheel and fourth wheel to the right, with the rest of the movement faded to a ghost behind them\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-09-27T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.09.27</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>28 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/watch-movement\">A watch that is not animated</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">The seconds hand moves because a balance wheel is vibrating, and for no other reason. Wind the crown, pull it out to set the time, put it on a wrist and let the rotor wind it for you, and fade the bridges away to watch the escapement lock, unlock and impulse five times a second.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Horology</li><li>3D</li><li>Javascript</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/solar-eclipses.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/solar-eclipses.webp\" alt=\"The solar eclipse app showing an annular eclipse shadow crossing South America\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-03-22T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.03.22</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/solar-eclipses\">Visualizing solar eclipses</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">A total eclipse is a cosmic coincidence: a moon that just barely covers the sun. This app lets you move through the Sun, Moon and Earth system and watch the geometry that decides which patch of the planet falls into shadow.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Javascript</li><li>Visualization</li><li>Astronomy</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/task-board.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/task-board.webp\" alt=\"A kanban board with cards spread across To Do, In Progress and Done\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2026-03-22T00:00:00.000Z\">2026.03.22</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/task-management\">Task management app</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">A lightweight, visual task board that runs entirely in the browser. Move work between columns, track what is in flight, and keep day-to-day planning low friction: no backend, no account, nothing to sync.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Javascript</li><li>React</li><li>Productivity</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/balanced-tree.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/balanced-tree.webp\" alt=\"A balanced binary tree built from twelve values, each node labelled with its height\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2020-04-09T00:00:00.000Z\">2020.04.09</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>2 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/balanced-tree\">Balanced binary tree animated</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">Balanced binary trees promise fast inserts, finds and deletes, and rotations are what keep the promise: they stop the tree from growing lopsided. Add and remove nodes here and watch each rotation play out one step at a time.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Javascript</li><li>CSS</li><li>Balanced Binary Tree</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/minesweeper.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/minesweeper.webp\" alt=\"An expert minesweeper board most of the way played out, with flagged mines\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2020-02-18T00:00:00.000Z\">2020.02.18</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/minesweeper\">Minesweeper</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">The classic sweep-for-mines game, rebuilt with React and plain CSS on top of a flood fill that opens up the empty regions. Same nerve-wracking first click, now with a seven-segment timer counting against you.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Minesweeper</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>\n<li>\n  <article class=\"trailer\">\n    <div class=\"trailer-media\">\n      <img class=\"trailer-media-blur\" src=\"/images/demos/todo-board.webp\" alt=\"\" aria-hidden=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n        <img class=\"trailer-media-img\" src=\"/images/demos/todo-board.webp\" alt=\"A three column todo board with items spread across Todo, Doing and Done\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" />\n      <span class=\"trailer-cat\">Blog</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"trailer-body\">\n      <p class=\"trailer-meta\">\n        <time datetime=\"2020-01-26T00:00:00.000Z\">2020.01.26</time>\n        <span aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n        <span>1 min read</span>\n      </p>\n      <h3 class=\"trailer-title\"><a href=\"/blog/reacttodolist\">Todo list with React and LocalStorage</a></h3>\n      <p class=\"trailer-text\">A todo list that lives entirely in your browser: React for the interface, localStorage for memory. Close the tab, come back next week, and the list is exactly where you left it.</p>\n      <ul class=\"trailer-tags\"><li>Javascript</li><li>React</li><li>CSS</li></ul>\n      <span class=\"trailer-cta\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Read article</span>\n    </div>\n  </article>\n</li>"}